  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nQuiet and pleasant Fall weather prevails through the work week\nand beyond into the weekend courtesy of strong high pressure\nboth aloft and at the surface. This pattern will continue to\npromote predominantly dry weather and diurnal trends remaining \nconsistent, with seasonable daytime highs and cool nighttime\nlows. \n\nThe orientation of the surface high will begin to yield a\nslight moderation to overnight temperatures, making frost\nformation more isolated in nature in comparison to past\nmornings. Did not see strong enough evidence for a Frost\nAdvisory tonight, but sheltered valleys in the northern lowlands\ncould see patchy frost development just before sunrise. Additionally,\nslightly breezy low level winds parked just above the surface \nwill stifle sufficient conditions needed river valley fog \nTuesday morning.\n\nForecast soundings for this week depict a deep layer of dry air\nretaining residency over the area. This will mix down to the\nsurface during peak heating hours each day, attributing to dew\npoints bottoming out in the 20s and 30s. Will have to remain\nvigilant to minimum RH values this week as leaf litter grows\nmore abundant, but for now do not foresee fire weather concerns\noutside of the higher terrain.",
